  "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $(32)$ by a negative one $(-9).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n32÷(-9)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $32$ by $9$ without any signs: $32÷9=3\\,\\frac{5}{9}.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n32÷(-9)=-3\\,\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$",
